RAG = Retrieval-Augmented Generation

RAG combines:

Retrieval + Generation

Instead of relying only on the LLM's training data:

User Question
 ↓
Retrieve relevant information
 ↓
Give information to LLM
 ↓
Generate answer
Example

Suppose you upload your company HR policy.

User:

How many casual leaves can I take?

RAG:

Question
 ↓
Embedding
 ↓
Vector DB
 ↓
Find HR policy
 ↓
Relevant paragraph
 ↓
LLM
 ↓
Answer
RAG pipeline
Documents
 ↓
Document Loader
 ↓
Text Splitting
 ↓
Embeddings
 ↓
Vector Database

Then:

User Query
 ↓
Query Embedding
 ↓
Similarity Search
 ↓
Retrieved Documents
 ↓
LLM
 ↓
Answer
